"""
sportst - a terminal scoreboard for the NFL, college football, the NBA,
men's college basketball, the NHL, the AHL, MLB, college baseball, and the
Winter and Summer Olympics.

Inspired by mlbt. Scores, scouting reports, box scores, plays (with clips of
scoring plays), standings, team and player stats, brackets with championship
odds, betting lines with value picks, and favourites - from free, public
sources: ESPN's public API, the AHL's HockeyTech feed, the NHL and MLB stats
APIs, NCAA.com, Action Network, Kalshi, YouTube channel feeds and Wikipedia.
Standard library only: no pip install, no virtualenv, no dependency drift.

Nothing personal ships with it. Your settings and favourite teams live in
~/.config/sportst/config.json, created the first time you change something:
on the Settings tab (O), on the Favorites tab (0), or with
`sportst --write-config` and a text editor.

    sportst              launch the full-screen app
    sportst --help       flags and one-shot printing modes
    ?                    key bindings, once you are inside
"""

